1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,180
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:16,940
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon. Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store. Until one night, he decided to rewrite his story.

3
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:29,640
And there was like one night, stay up all night long, and rather than give myself excuses, I would look at everything that I'm up in my life or everything I'm not doing or whatever, and just not give myself any excuses out.

4
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,620
Just like nail it.

5
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,580
And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

6
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,660
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

7
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:42,480
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep.

8
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,700
I decided to change my life.

9
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,060
Today I present you the Tarantino method.

10
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,580
To follow this process you'll need three things.

11
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:51,000
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

12
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,560
When the world is silent and not a soul is awake.

13
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,020
That's when it can happen.

14
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:55,760
Trust.

15
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:56,840
Now it begins.

16
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,920
The first page is always going to be the hardest.

17
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:03,180
But it's really all about getting that ball rolling.

18
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:08,680
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear-mongering question.

19
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:18,927
What am I doing wrong Be brutally honest As Quinton himself would say nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough

20
00:01:18,927 --> 00:01:19,927
But it's absolutely necessary.

21
00:01:19,927 --> 00:01:23,927
And when you push through, boom, you're halfway there.

22
00:01:26,927 --> 00:01:27,927
It's all out there.

23
00:01:27,927 --> 00:01:33,927
The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out bare for you to

24
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:34,927
see.

25
00:01:34,927 --> 00:01:37,927
Not built up in your mind, but on paper, tangible.

26
00:01:37,927 --> 00:01:43,847
Take a moment, because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

27
00:01:44,307 --> 00:01:48,327
We're not all Quentin Tarantino. You might be feeling like you're all written out.

28
00:01:48,727 --> 00:01:51,767
So let's make this part simple. A straightforward list.

29
00:01:52,247 --> 00:01:54,187
A hundred ways you can change your life.

30
00:01:54,187 --> 00:01:59,127
Quite a simple process. Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it.

31
00:01:59,727 --> 00:02:06,627
Repeat it over and over again. Push forward. Write it down. Adapt. Reflect. Learn. And grow.

32
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:10,367
Until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my life?

33
00:02:10,487 --> 00:02:11,827
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

34
00:02:11,927 --> 00:02:15,367
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

35
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:17,147
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
